lj.

# Rationality fixture: self-attack (odd loop of length 1).
# One argument for P resting on the negation-as-failure default for P itself:
# pRule needs P->false on the term side, derived from a geled for P.
# Expected grounded labelling (graph labeller, see README.org):
#   node P: UNDEC on both sides; the argument's presumption site is UNDEC.

declare P:bool.
declare pRule : ((P->false)->P).

start argument SelfAttack P
cut ((P->false)->P) rule.
axiom pRule.
elim.
elim h.
cut (P) alpha.
axiom h.
by default.
next.
axiom.
end argument

% D0 (2026-09-16): the self-attacking argument compiles as the cyclic
% edge P[t] <- P[c]:pres; preferred/stable label P[t] OUT, P[c] IN.
% The evaluation is a value polynomial in the presumption: the defeat
% comes from the contrariness guard, not from a scaffold, so nothing in
% the term reflects it (recorded under aida-cyclic-fragment).
graph SelfAttack
label SelfAttack preferred
evaluate SelfAttack credulous
